./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_15_yaw_aug_claude/yaw_aug_codex_code_evalr2_review.md:50:All four E1 findings are closed by `ef362c2`:
./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:103:**Launcher `depth_canon_launch.sh`** — adapted from the reviewed exp_17 launcher with its r3 blocking findings applied AND the review-H9 gates: (1) reviewed-tree binding: pin **HEAD** and content-pin every file on the training path (`train.py`, `defaults.ini`, `src/data/*.py`, `src/models/*.py`, `src/training/*.py`, `src/inference/*.py`, `AR_md.py`, dataset config, split, VAE, control + arm config, the DINOv3 gate script) via a committed manifest; (2) smoke evidence must carry the same HEAD + manifest hash + `config contract OK`, and **a smoke is re-run after any review-driven source change**; (3) no `pipefail` around `tr | grep` — the log is read once into a variable after `wait`-draining the `tee` FIFO; (4) NaN/Inf check in FULL mode too; (5) **run-owned checkpoints**: FULL refuses a non-empty run namespace, every accepted checkpoint must be newer than the launch epoch, the cadence set must be exactly {2500, …, 40000}, foreign/stale files abort; (6) **NAS gate on the save filesystem**: mount identity (`findmnt`/`df` of the save path shows the CIFS share), a write-probe file, free space ≥ 30 GiB; (7) pinned smoke-projection threshold ≤ 60 h (**v14:** ≤ 120 h, because a shared card roughly halves the uncontended 0.259 opt-steps/s — the bound is a sanity cap on a co-tenant launch, not a speed target; **v15:** ≤ 300 h — SMOKE 2 (2026-10-26 05:38 EDT, `d838c8e`) measured the real contended rate next to two 100 %-utilization xRIR trainings: 19.27 s/step, ≈ 5× the uncontended 3.86 s/step, projected 214.1 h, so v14's 2× assumption was wrong by 2.5×; under `shared` the projection measures the co-tenants' load at that moment, which relaxes as they finish (their checkpoint cadence put GPU 0 free ≈ Oct 26 midday and GPU 1 ≈ Oct 27 05:00 EDT), so the cap keeps only its sanity role — 300 h ≈ 7× the uncontended 43 h still catches an order-of-magnitude pathology; the contended rate is disclosed in the evidence and the result tables as speed-only); **v10 (Codex r3b):** (8) GPU gate = ≥ 22.5 GiB free on BOTH cards **and zero foreign compute processes** on GPUs 0/1 (`nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps`; HIGH 7) — the launcher kills nothing; **v11:** every nvidia-smi query is strict (exit status checked apart from stdout, exactly one numeric memory row per card, malformed or unknown-uuid rows refuse) and every GPU-gate refusal exits with the DEDICATED **rc 7** (the watcher's only transient signal); **v12 (Codex rA2 HIGH 1/2):** rc 7 is emitted by ONE function (`gpu_refuse`) and an EXIT trap remaps any other exit 7 — `train.py`'s own status included — to the terminal **rc 8**, so a trainer failure is never retried; after the gate the co-tenancy disclosure issues NO further nvidia-smi query (it prints the strict gate's validated answers: free MiB + uuid per card, compute processes on other cards). **v14 (SHARED-GPU launch mode, ordered by Yixun 2026-10-25 ≈ 22:40 EDT — verbatim "please launch exp_25 if we have enough GPU free usage", then the AskUserQuestion choice "Relax the gates and launch shared now"):** the gate is MEMORY-ONLY: pinned `MIN_GPU_FREE_MIB=12288` (12 GiB per card; measured need of the identical `--batch-size 32 --num-gpus 2` recipe on this box: 5.9–6.6 GiB per rank in exp_14's smoke, ≈ 10.3 GiB per card for the exp_13 vanilla-B arm; the old 22.5 GiB floor was a margin, never a measurement), pinned `GPU_OCCUPANCY_POLICY=shared` (the other value, `idle`, restores the v10 refusal), the strict nvidia-smi parsing of v11 kept in full; foreign compute processes on GPU 0/1 are DISCLOSED (pid, card, used MiB, cwd) in the launch log and in the SMOKE evidence (`gpu_policy`, `min_gpu_free_mib`, `free_mib_at_launch`, `co_tenants_at_launch`) instead of refused; rc 7 stays reserved for the memory floor and unclean queries. Consequences carried as result disclosures: the FULL run and the campaign execute next to Yixun's xRIR exp_13/exp_28 chains (32 GiB each, 100 % utilization) and user dzheng's lanes — speed only, never the numbers; OOM risk in both directions (a co-tenant growing past the free memory kills whichever process allocates last; this launcher still never signals anything); the watcher's poll predicate mirrors the policy (foreign processes logged, memory floor decides). The eval campaign runs its lanes with `ALLOW_SHARED_GPU=1` (A6 opt-in, exercised by this instruction). Launcher exit codes: 0 ok · 2 a gate refused · 3 banner missing · 4 non-finite / SMOKE verdict FAILED · 5 checkpoint set wrong · 6 endpoint or two-rank start missing · 7 GPU gate (transient) · 8 a remapped 7 · anything else = `train.py`'s own status; (9) the interpreter is **enforced** (`command -v python` must resolve under `envs/flac/bin`; HIGH 6); (10) **tie-audit gate (BLOCKING 1; v11 = Codex rA A1 + rB B1):** SMOKE and FULL both refuse unless the committed, PINNED rung-3 audit report `depth_canon_tie_audit.json` + `.sha256` (in the pin set, committed at HEAD) passes THE one predicate `depth_canon_audit_gate.py` (`validate_tie_audit(audit_path, repo_root) -> (ok, problems, summary)`; CLI 0/1/2): sidecar, type-strict schema, `verdict PASS`, zero survivors/errors, full non-`--limit` coverage of the three splits, registered item counts, `dirty_code == ""`, no harness tag in production, the expected 9,650 unique map paths derived from the split JSONs through the audit script's own enumeration (path-set equality, no duplicates, typed rows), per-split census consistent with the rows, content hashes of the audit script / operator / `dataset.py` / `AR_md.py` / dataset configs / split JSONs, and a **re-hash of every current depth map** against the row hashes (8 threads inside a KILLABLE child process — the gate itself in `--rehash-worker` mode, own session — under the registered **900 s** wall-clock deadline `REHASH_DEADLINE_S`, no CLI or env override; read-only NAS, ≈ 2 min 15 s per launch; a timeout SIGKILLs the child's process group and fails closed, as do a nonzero child, no JSON or a malformed answer → launcher rc 2 → watcher FAILED; v12, Codex rA2 NIT 4). The gate module's sha256 joins the SMOKE→FULL content bind. Harness mode accepts a harness-tagged synthetic report only under `DEPTH_CANON_HARNESS` against a harness-provided contract file; (11) **SMOKE evidence (BLOCKING 2):** mandatory parsed finite loss and the wrapper's rank-0 fit-end line `canonicalize latency rank0 batches=<int> samples=<int> total_s=<float> mean_ms_per_batch=<float>` (no `null` fields); (12) the SMOKE→FULL bind is **content-scoped** (NIT): FULL requires the smoke's pin-manifest sha256 and training-closure content to equal the current tree's, so record-only commits between SMOKE and FULL are safe, while `EXPECT_HEAD` stays HEAD-identity for the launch itself (hence the freeze rule in §11 A5). Pin closure adds `FLAC_AR_BV.json` / `FLAC_AR_BF.json` (opened by the DINOv3 gate; HIGH 5) and, in v11, the committed tie-audit report + sidecar → **48 entries**; `assert_arm_configs.py::assert_vit_pin` now hash-pins the whole DINOv3 snapshot file set incl. `config.json` (Codex rA H5). W&B writes a repo-local `wandb/` directory (gitignored) — documented, not a gate. MODE=SMOKE (25 steps, cadence 10⁶ ⇒ no checkpoint, own namespace) → MODE=FULL requires a passing SMOKE on record. Guard suite `depth_canon_guardtests.sh` drives the launcher's real branches with `DRY_RUN=1` and synthetic logs in `mktemp -d` — never the production evidence directory.
./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:188:9. **Recovery (v13; Yixun A8 + integrative review HIGH 2):** the launcher has NO gated resume MODE (P1 recipe: no `--ckpt-path`; FULL requires an empty namespace; the checkpoint-set gate assumes one launch marker), so an ad-hoc autonomous resume is NOT performed. If FULL crashes: prove no rank or launcher remains; preserve the namespace + logs; identify the latest complete 2,500-step boundary (bytes, sha256, length, step, parent launch marker, parent manifest); then resume ONLY through a reviewed path — preferably a `MODE=RESUME` launcher extension (TDD + guard cases + Codex review; built after FULL has launched, since the branch is frozen until then) or, if the crash precedes it, the six-step manual prescription kept in the FLAC-checkout HANDOFF (every pre-launch gate re-run by hand incl. the audit re-hash, NAS, W&B, DINO/init and strict two-GPU occupancy right before launch; the exact recipe with ONLY `--ckpt-path <verified boundary>` added, 40k endpoint / cadence / offline kept, a resume marker, a fresh W&B run id with the parent recorded; the same banner / both-rank / finite-loss / endpoint / tie-count / latency / checkpoint-ownership / exact-byte checks with tie + latency totals aggregated across legs; ONE explicit CANON lineage manifest — original hashes through boundary N, resumed hashes after N, no duplicate or foreign step, endpoint included — passed explicitly to the collector; full disclosure of crash, boundary, parent/child identities and the RNG/dataloader discontinuity). A resumed CANON arm remains a historical matched-recipe comparison (P1 itself resumed at 32.5k) but not a bit-identical trajectory pair.
